------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                      CODING RULES FOR stdlib_*.asm FILES
                for automatic generation of the '.depends' file
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1) CODE STRUCTURE FOR A GENERIC Routine(i):

      !ifdef caml_PRIM__<ROUTINE_LABEL(i)> '{'
      <ROUTINE_LABEL(i)>
          <acme_code>
      [<GLOBAL_LABEL(i,1)> ['=' <acme_expr>]]
          <acme_code>
          ...
      [<GLOBAL_LABEL(i,n)> ['=' <acme_expr>]]
          <acme_code>
          [<FALLTHROUGH_COMMENT> <ROUTINE_LABEL(i+1)>]
      '}'

 · <ROUTINE_LABEL(i)>    ::= /caml_<NAME>/
   The label for the main entry point of Routine(i).

 · <GLOBAL_LABEL(i,x)>   ::= /<ROUTINE_LABEL(i)>__<NAME>/
   The x-th global label defined in Routine(i); note the TWO underscores.

 · <NAME>                ::= /[a-zA-Z](_?[a-zA-Z0-9])*/
   One or more alphanumeric strings, separated by a SINGLE underscore; the
   first string must begin with a letter.

 · <FALLTHROUGH_COMMENT> ::= /;+<SPC>*<FT_TXT><SPC>+<ROUTINE_LABEL(i+1)>/
   The comment regarding the fallthrough point to Routine(i+1).

 · <FT_TEXT>             ::= /fallthrough/ (case insensitive)
 · <SPC>                 ::= /[ \t]/       (space or tab)

 · The final  closing curly brace  must be in the  FIRST COLUMN; no  other '}'
   within <acme_code> may be in the first column.

 · If  a  fallthrough point  is  present,  it MUST  be  commented  out with  a
   <FALLTHROUGH_COMMENT>; the comment must PRECEDE the final closing '}'.

 · DO  NOT  refer,  within  <acme_code>  or  <acme_expr>  of  Routine(i)>,  to
   zone-local  symbols   (labels  beginning  with  '.')   defined  in  another
   Routine(j), or to  global symbols that do not conform  to the definition of
   <GLOBAL_LABEL(j,_)>. Better yet, avoid using them altogether.

 · All characters from the leftmost ';' to the end of the line will be treated
   as comments and  ignored, even if the  ';' is enclosed in  single or double
   quotes:

   .BAD:  LDA #';':JSR caml_my_routine  ;this dependency WILL NOT BE DETECTED!
   .GOOD: LDA #';'
          JSR caml_my_routine           ;this dependency will be detected.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2) HOW DEPENDENCIES ARE DETECTED BY mkdepends:

 · Any occurrence of <ROUTINE_LABEL(j)>  or <GLOBAL_LABEL(j,_)> in <acme_code>
   or <acme_expr> will be treated as a dependency of Routine(i) on Routine(j),
   where j <> i.

 · A <FALLTHROUGH_COMMENT>  will be treated  as a dependency of  Routine(i) on
   Routine(i+1).

 · After identifying  the set of  all dependencies, the script  calculates its
   transitive  closure   and  generates  the  complete   list  of  conditional
   assignments required for the correct assembly of each routine.

